# Design System 2.0

Longhua is one commercial product. UI has a single source of truth:

`src/design-system/`

## Rules

- New screens and new UI in existing screens MUST compose from `@/design-system`.
- Do NOT invent new button/card/badge/empty/loading/error visuals "on the page".
- Do NOT copy class stacks from old pages into new work.
- Do NOT add Button variants outside `src/design-system/primitives/Button.jsx`.
- Prefer `@/design-system` over direct `@/components/ui/*` imports in **new** code.
- Domain cards stay presentational (props in) — no API calls inside `design-system/domain/`.
- Spacing uses the 8pt grid (`tokens/spacing`, `--lh-space-*`).
- Icons use size tokens (`sm|md|lg|xl`) — no ad-hoc `h-4 w-4` in new code.
- `apps/mobile` is NOT a second product UI (see ADR-001). Do not grow feature parity there.

## Allowed exceptions

- Temporary edits inside not-yet-migrated legacy pages may touch local styles, but any **new** control must still come from the Design System when practical.
- Jitsi SDK wiring, E2EE crypto, and raw canvas/WebRTC host nodes are not DS concerns.

